		why: "THE PROMISE (kit.ts:228): \"Envelope fields common to every mutation: bump revision + updated-by/at (and optionally semanticVersion).\" The optional semanticVersion limb is what a caller opts into via advanceStatus's `bumpSemanticVersion`. WHO RELIES ON IT: JPWB-DOC-003 DEC-2, quoted at the victim's head — \"Revising a decomposition is legal, changes the parent's semantic version, and triggers impact analysis\" — discharged by `reviseDecomposition` (decomposition.ts:483-497), which is `advanceStatus` with `bumpSemanticVersion: true`. WHAT THE MUTATION DOES TO THEM: the committed STATE keeps the value spread in from `...current` (1) while commitState still bumps the STORE ROW to 2 via its own `newSemanticVersion`. The two then disagree silently — a reader taking the object's semantic version from its state sees a revision that did not happen, and DEC-2's \"changes the parent's semantic version\" is satisfied in the row and violated in the object. ⚠ ONLY ONE OF THIS FUNCTION'S THREE LIMBS IS GUARDED BY THIS ENTRY, and the other two are recorded as OPEN rather than closed: (a) `revision: newRevision` written into object STATE — the triage reports no reader anywhere (every revision read it found takes StoredObject.revision), so a mutant there should be expected to SURVIVE; (b) `updatedAt`/`updatedBy` — production-consumed (floor-gate.ts:240 and apps/rph-demo/src/lib/server/floor.ts:485 select the latest floor assessment by `state.updatedAt`) but asserted nowhere, every handler suite stamping one constant timestamp. ⛔ I did not re-run either claim; they are carried forward from the triage UNVERIFIED and must be measured before being relied on.\n\nOBSERVED: decomposition-revise-conformance.test.ts 4/4 PASS -> 3 pass / 1 fail. Killing assertion :205 `expect(h.stateOf(DCP).semanticVersion).toBe(2)` -> AssertionError: expected 1 to be 2. The reddened test is the file's CONTROL (\"an ordinary revision still supersedes, so the guard refuses only what it must\"). Note which assertion does NOT redden and why it matters: :194 `expect(payload.semanticVersion).toBe(h.stateOf(DCP).semanticVersion)` stays GREEN because under the mutant both sides fall to 1 together — it compares two derived values, so only :205's literal is load-bearing here. Mutant compiles (dropping the spread leaves `newSemanticVersion` an unused parameter; base.json sets neither noUnusedLocals nor noUnusedParameters, verified by running tsc). Anchor: 1 hit, lines 238-239, OWNERS [\"nextEnvelope\"] (span 229-242); the second line is carried so the replacement effects a deletion while staying invertible.",
