		why: "THE PROMISE (kit.ts:558-559): \"Build the shared envelope fields for a NEW object (revision 0, semanticVersion 1). Callers merge their object-specific fields (including the typed lifecycle field) on top\" — including the ProvenanceRecord whose `sourceObjectIds` the caller supplies. What that binding carries is stated at the call site, artifact.ts:39-40: \"`sourceObjectIds` binds the producers DOC-009 §18.1 names — producing PWU and producing Execution Attempt. The corpus attributes an artifact to those two and never to the Execution Step.\" WHO RELIES ON IT: newEnvelope has 29 production call sites across 17 handler files (artifact, assurance ×5, decomposition ×2, execution, governance ×3, pwa-authoring ×4, product-behavior ×5, runtime-binding, model-exchange, harness, deferral, obligation-constraint ×2, context-assembly-policy); `recordArtifact` (artifact.ts:52-55) is the site that passes a NON-EMPTY set. WHAT THE MUTATION DOES TO THEM: discarding the caller's ids makes every new object a lineage ROOT. The provenance record is still present and still valid — `sourceObjectIds: []` is exactly what a legitimately root object looks like — so an artifact that HAS producers becomes indistinguishable from one that has none, and DOC-009 §18.1's attribution is lost without any schema complaining. ⚠ NEAR MISS RECORDED, because it is the mis-attribution this programme has paid for before: pwu-nothing-inferred.test.ts:633-641 reads like the ideal precise assertion for this function's ontology spread, but `proposePwu` HAND-BUILDS its envelope inline (pwu.ts:297-311) and never calls newEnvelope — crediting that assertion here would have produced a survivor.\n\nOBSERVED: artifact.test.ts 6/6 PASS -> 5 pass / 1 fail. Killing assertion :98 `expect((s.provenance as { sourceObjectIds?: string[] }).sourceObjectIds).toEqual([PWU, ATTEMPT])` -> AssertionError: expected [] to deeply equal [ …(2) ]. The reddened test is the one whose name states the promise: \"binds the producers DOC-009 §18.1 names — the PWU and the Execution Attempt, never the step\". The other 5 hold, including :97 `expect(s.provenance).toBeDefined()` — so the mutant discriminates the BINDING from the mere presence of a provenance record. Mutant compiles. Anchor: 1 hit, line 586, OWNERS [\"newEnvelope\"] (span 560-594).",
